# The refusal names the declaration, the SOURCE ROLE the evaluation plan carried (not the minted binding id), the
# offending type and the suspension the value spans. The role NAMES the value, so the minted local name is absent:
# `the argument 's' of 'suspendPlanByRefLikeLen' has type`, not
# `... of 'suspendPlanByRefLikeLen' \`cir$b1\` has type`.
suspend-lowering: in `SuspendPlanBindingByRefLikeKt.suspendPlanByRefLikeSpanArgumentAcrossSuspension`
the argument 's' of 'suspendPlanByRefLikeLen' has type
which is byref-like (a `ref struct`, via `System.Span`)
lives across the suspending call to `suspendPlanByRefLikeRelay`
(mirrors C# CS4007)
